-- two reports on one material in one bath with different values: no function of the material and the bath
-- agrees with both. This is reports-disagree-no-function with the bath moved into the hypothesis, and the
-- move is the point. That statement convicted every disagreement alike, so it convicted a
-- variable-temperature series, a titration and a chiral-solvent experiment along with a contradiction. Two
-- reports have to agree on their bath before their disagreement means anything. The Classification and
-- Labelling Inventory's notifications are of that kind -- one substance, one hazard class, one set of
-- criteria, two answers.
breports-same-bath-disagree : (k : Material) → (v : Bath) → (r1 : BReport Nat) → (r2 : BReport Nat) → br-material Nat r1 ≡ k → br-material Nat r2 ≡ k → br-bath Nat r1 ≡ v → br-bath Nat r2 ≡ v → (br-value Nat r1 ≡ br-value Nat r2 → Empty) → ((h : Material → Bath → Nat) → ((r : BReport Nat) → h (br-material Nat r) (br-bath Nat r) ≡ br-value Nat r) → Empty)
breports-same-bath-disagree k v r1 r2 q1 q2 p1 p2 no =
  λ h → λ agrees → no (concat (sym (agrees r1)) (concat (cong-material-bath h (br-material Nat r1) k q1 (br-bath Nat r1) v p1) (concat (cong-material-bath h k (br-material Nat r2) (sym q2) v (br-bath Nat r2) (sym p2)) (agrees r2))))
